morse: fix RCU stall deadlock in morse_skbq_skb_finish TX status path

The morse_skbq_tx_status_process() function calls morse_skbq_skb_finish()
while holding mq->lock (spin_lock_bh). Inside __skbq_data_tx_finish(),
MORSE_IEEE80211_TX_STATUS() is called which invokes mac80211's
ieee80211_tx_status(). When A-MPDU aggregation is active, mac80211 may
call ieee80211_send_bar() from within the tx_status callback, which
re-enters the driver's ops_tx() -> morse_skbq_skb_tx() -> morse_skbq_tx()
and attempts to acquire the same mq->lock, causing a deadlock on the
singlethread MorseNetWorkQ workqueue. Since the workqueue thread never
yields, this manifests as an RCU self-detected stall on the CPU.

Fix by splitting the TX status processing in morse_skbq_tx_status_process:
1. Perform the skb unlink from the pending queue and header removal
   while holding the spinlock.
2. Release the spinlock.
3. Call morse_skbq_skb_finish() with the skb already detached.

To make step 3 safe, add a check in __skbq_data_tx_finish: if the skb
is already unlinked (next == NULL), skip the unlink call.

This patch only modifies morse driver code (skbq.c) and has no effect
on other wireless drivers (mt7996, ath, etc.) or their 2.4G/5G behavior.

Signed-off-by: EdgeCore <dev@edge-core.com>

--- a/skbq.c
+++ b/skbq.c
@@ -480,14 +480,22 @@ static void morse_skbq_tx_status_process
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Unlink from pending queue while holding the lock, so that
+		 * morse_skbq_skb_finish -> __skbq_data_tx_finish sees the skb
+		 * already detached and skips its own unlink.
+		 */
+		__morse_skbq_unlink(mq, &mq->pending, tx_skb);
+
 		morse_skb_remove_hdr_after_sent_to_chip(tx_skb);
 
-		if (is_fullmac_mode())
+		spin_unlock_bh(&mq->lock);
+
+		if (is_fullmac_mode()) {
 			morse_skbq_skb_finish_fullmac(mq, tx_skb, tx_sts);
-		else
+		} else {
 			morse_skbq_skb_finish(mq, tx_skb, tx_sts);
-
-		spin_unlock_bh(&mq->lock);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (mors->cfg->ops->skbq_get_tx_buffered_count(mors) == 0) {
@@ -1228,7 +1236,13 @@ static int __skbq_data_tx_finish(struct
 	if (morse_skbq_mon)
 		morse_skbq_mon_adjust(mors, skb, 0);
 
-	__morse_skbq_unlink(mq, &mq->pending, skb);
+	/*
+	 * If the caller already unlinked the skb (e.g. morse_skbq_tx_status_process
+	 * to avoid holding the lock across ieee80211_tx_status), the skb will not
+	 * be on any queue. Check before unlinking to avoid list corruption.
+	 */
+	if (skb->next != NULL)
+		__morse_skbq_unlink(mq, &mq->pending, skb);
 
 	/* Workaround Linux */
 	__skbq_qosnullfunc_to_nullfunc(skb);
